   $q$The passage ends by saying the project succeeded more because of shared work than technology. Which detail gives the strongest support for that view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The mesh is fine plastic stretched between two tall poles.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"},{"text":"Wind and dust damage the nets, so residents take turns inspecting and patching them weekly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"By 2019, twelve nets were supplying water to the school kitchen.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Quispe moved every net uphill after the first season's results.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Wind and dust damage the nets, so residents take turns inspecting and patching them weekly.$q$, $q$The fourth paragraph shows the nets break down without regular care, and the community's weekly rotation keeps them working, which is exactly the shared work Quispe credits. Moving the nets uphill was one engineer's decision, so it supports good planning rather than community effort.$q$, 'draft', '0ec8b0a6-0340-5453-893b-b7accb5a698a')
