   $q$According to the passage, how did Halvering decide when it was noon in the 1850s?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It used a timetable printed by the town newspaper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It followed the clock in the railroad office near the river.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-time-period"},{"text":"It rang the bell when the sun stood highest over the courthouse.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It copied the time used in Brookmoor, forty miles east.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It rang the bell when the sun stood highest over the courthouse.$q$, $q$The first paragraph states that "when the sun stood highest over the courthouse, the town bell rang noon." The railroad office clock became the standard only later, after 1863.$q$, 'draft', 'e3405368-081a-51b6-b988-0898f1d0d17e')
