   $q$Based on the passage, why did the researchers also count moths visiting meadow flowers?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To find out which flowers moths prefer when no lights are present.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To learn whether lights pulling moths away affected the pollination of nearby plants.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To check whether the moth traps were working correctly on both roads.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To prove that amber lamps make flowers produce more seeds than before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstatement"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To learn whether lights pulling moths away affected the pollination of nearby plants.$q$, $q$The passage links lamps drawing insects "away from the meadows" to flower visits and notes that fewer visits "may mean fewer seeds." It never claims amber lamps increased seeds; flower visits on that road simply "stayed nearly the same."$q$, 'draft', 'be6f3449-9508-5af4-ba78-21ded9c58cc3')
