   $q$Which evidence best explains why the even-pace group finished faster?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They improved by eleven seconds on their timed two-kilometer test.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-result"},{"text":"Several of them said the even pace felt too slow at the start.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"They used less power early but kept much more of their power in the final minute.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They produced less power in the first minute than the other group did.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They used less power early but kept much more of their power in the final minute.$q$, $q$The power readings show the even-pace rowers saved energy early and held more power at the end, which explains the faster time. The eleven-second improvement is the result itself, not the explanation for it.$q$, 'draft', '1d9751b5-86a6-595d-9244-70f23204d3ab')
