  ('7a167268-0a6b-5d1e-8b39-545c47864170', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Based on the passage, what is the key difference between a "best by" date and a "use by" date?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Best by\" usually concerns quality, while \"use by\" calls for closer attention to safety.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Best by\" means food is unsafe the next day, while \"use by\" is only a suggestion.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-relationship"},{"text":"\"Best by\" applies to canned goods, while \"use by\" applies to fresh produce.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"\"Best by\" is set by health offices, while \"use by\" is set by stores.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Best by" usually concerns quality, while "use by" calls for closer attention to safety.$q$, $q$The passage says "best by" usually refers to "quality, such as flavor or crispness, rather than safety," while "use by" foods "deserve closer attention." The third choice repeats the families' mistaken belief that the passage corrects.$q$, 'draft', '302f1042-d238-54e1-9bc9-79b37baae6d8')
