   $q$Which result most directly shows that the guide changed how families used date labels?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The students hope to give their guide to grocery stores.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Items discarded only because of the printed date dropped by nearly half.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The class surveyed 150 households for one week.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"describes-method"},{"text":"Families reported throwing away about a quarter less food overall.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-vague"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Items discarded only because of the printed date dropped by nearly half.$q$, $q$The drop in items thrown out "only because of the printed date" measures the exact behavior the guide targeted. The overall drop of a quarter could include other changes, so it is less direct evidence.$q$, 'draft', '302f1042-d238-54e1-9bc9-79b37baae6d8')
